#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:5
#: 0222e1084b9a4028b1b37ee3af72f18a
msgid "Crossfire and ELRS RC Systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:7
#: 535bff6094ca4cef83fd4094ec637bd3
msgid "Any Crossfire/ELRS compatible receiver can be used with ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:9
#: 4b32f0ea5d964b55a7a69b491e934123
msgid "ELRS (ExpressLRS) RC systems use the CRSF protocol and are connected in a similar manner as Crossfire receivers to an autopilot UART. ELRS can also be configured to be MAVLink protocol with embedded RC control (See below). On  F4/F7 based autopilots the UART MUST be DMA enabled for reliable operation in CRSF protocol mode. Consult :ref:`common-autopilots`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:11
#: fe6afffd7dc545f9b43ff1c7c650bcae
msgid "If you do not wish to use telemetry then a TBS Crossfire or ELRS receiver can be connected to the **RCIN** port using :ref:`SBUS <common-rc-systems>`. You must configure the receiver to output SBUS, of course."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:15
#: eb667c9bacc24c6da68e05cf958fc4d3
msgid "CRSF Receivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:17
#: 447d2265f09c49e489242e253192f22d
msgid "If you wish to use telemetry then a receiver can be connected to a UART utilizing the `CRSF <https://www.team-blacksheep.com/products/prod:crossfire_tx>`__ protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:19
#: e165e7b378ed4fd485aa68cde3db5612
msgid "CRSF is a full-duplex protocol that supports integrated telemetry and a number of other features. Connect the RX pin of the UART to the CRSF TX pin of the CRSF device and vice versa. Currently a full-duplex UART connection is required. For best performance a UART with DMA capability on its RX port is desirable, but not required. A message will be displayed once on the GCS console, if connected to a UART without this capability on an F4/F7 based autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:22
#: bf2b4e5aaa004652ac61a72da8477f23
msgid "In the configuration of the serial port select the RCIN protocol. So for example for serial port 4:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:24
#: 155a207d28cb4888a85570cb37058192
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL <SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` = 23"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:25
#: 06ac9efd7831471ca9f987d49e0798eb
msgid "Set :ref:`RSSI_TYPE <RSSI_TYPE>` = 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:27
#: 7d7741e20b5c4aa0bb0cb14e75451162
msgid "The serial port baudrate is automatically set and controlled by the firmware when any serial RC protocol, such as CRSF, is detected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:29
#: 3db912b3c3374af3bbc3d1462c52f762
msgid "With the receiver connected and configured correctly proceed with RC calibration as normal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:31
#: 75ca03be594f43bf9e9c387dc1efa39f
msgid "See :ref:`common-crsf-telemetry` for information about telemetry data sent, display scripts for OpenTX transmitters, and adjustment of ArduPilot parameters via CRSF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:33
#: f4bb03a051bd44478a1a0346e8f72d6d
msgid "If the autopilot is rebooted via MAVLink, it will lose communication with the CRSF receiver until the receiver is power cycled. Also, the CRSF TX must be transmitting BEFORE the receiver is powered up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:36
#: 927f0950e2074975b275d6828bb02621
msgid "MAVLink Option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:38
#: d55e2307db264a33a8c16970613eba87
msgid "In addition to SBUS and CRSF protocols, CRSF receivers can be configured to use MAVLink protocol for telemetry and embedded RC control. To utilize this attach to SERIAL port 4(as an example) and configure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:40
#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:56
#: b663c151ff444244936d59e77bfb4fea
#: 576227bc17a4484e9d33ddd0d5cd6c11
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL <SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` = 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:41
#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:57
#: 173d858d701a4e4c8a868f3ab1b2b42c
#: 9fe8501b9056434f96ec12383e7cfa93
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL4_BAUD <SERIAL4_BAUD>` = 115"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:42
#: 12085951294344d6bb797a446dd8a717
msgid "Set :ref:`RSSI_TYPE <RSSI_TYPE>` =  5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:45
#: f5ce46cfa88348afa1173f6e7d154b68
msgid "ELRS Receivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:47
#: afe7811c021545699335aa31359f6500
msgid "ELRS can be setup in the same manner as CRSF above , however, bit 13 of :ref:`RC_OPTIONS<RC_OPTIONS>` should be set to alter the baudrate from 416KBaud that CRSF uses, to 420KBaud that ELRS uses when in CRSF compatible protocol mode. As mentioned above, the UART selected must have DMA capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:49
#: 8a94548bf649435fafeb4d10f311b4e4
msgid "ELRS can also be configured to output MAVLink, enabling full bidirectional Mavlink telemetry and RC control over the same link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:52
#: 78b328b08bdf4675afa2d2713ca4c9de
msgid "ELRS MAVLink Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:54
#: b948f8e7a7e348c88ea2aa7a0dc9d219
msgid "Instead of CRSF protocol, MAVLink protocol can be used if the receiver is configured for it. In this case, using SERIAL 4 for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:58
#: bff1b919e5444890bdfcd640e1a26791
msgid "Set :ref:`RSSI_TYPE <RSSI_TYPE>` = 5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:60
#: 3ee180fb38ec41a4a3c3400bb3f743c4
msgid "If the ELRS transmitter module has WIFI capability, then the telemetry data can be forwarded wirelessly to a PC or phone based GCS close to the transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:63
#: 48030a23598a42b5a7ddf59aa1f1c13f
msgid "ELRS bootloader \"lockup\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:65
#: b4820a02d0394fdaa49ae03dfc37d126
msgid "Some ELRS receivers can appear to be locked up in \"bootloader\" mode when the autopilot system is powered on. This is usually due to the UART RX pin to which they are attached being held low during power application, which ELRS interprets as being forced into bootloader mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:67
#: 51d6bd78d87b479e97cba93de37746c4
msgid "The most common cause for this is when the autopilot board also has a DJI HD VTX attached and the SBUS pin of that interface is directly tied to the UART RX pin being used for RC input from the ELRS. If the VTX is not powered up at the same time as the ELRS, the SBUS output will act as a current sink for the ELRS TX pin and force it into bootloader. This occurs if the autopilot is only being powered from USB or the autopilot bootloader forces the HD VTX power supply off on boot(so that the pilot must toggle a transmitter switch to actively turn it on, for power/heat saving). The simple solution is to remove the SBUS wire going from the HD VTX to the DJI connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:70
#: e9b108ccca1f47b4b90ac585f27a067b
msgid "CRSF Video Transmitters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:72
#: 66afc4781b4346e0bc2ba40ff06fd941
msgid "TBS Video Transmitters can also be connected to ArduPilot using the CRSF protocol. This allows the VTX to be configured via parameters and, for VTXs such as the `TBS Unify Evo <https://www.team-blacksheep.com/products/prod:tbs_unify_evo>`__ , receive telemetry data that can be displayed using the built-in OSD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:74
#: b84d52f4b13d4fb4906c28c3a9e01157
msgid "If you are using CRSF for RC input as well then nothing more needs to be done in order to enable VTX control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:76
#: 1ed3f541d0464911adeffc449022308b
msgid "If you only wish to use CRSF for VTX control then connect the VTX to the UART in the normal way - TX to RX and RX to TX and configure the UART connection as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:78
#: b53b680c6ce44867a3a1cc015437efb2
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL <SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` = 29"
msgstr ""
